Consumer threads plus limits plus fork plus untrusted plus sensitive plus
retries plus Code-Scanning plus sequential plus tag plus release stay
qualified with fixture evidence (issue #509).

Threads are replyable/resolvable PR review threads for diff-mapped
findings with one integration-owned updated summary comment per PR.
There is no review-comment opt-out or annotation-only mode. Deduplicate
integration-owned findings across reruns and bind new comments to the
analyzed revision. Preserve human comments, replies, and unrelated
threads. Keep a thread while its finding remains. When a later complete
assessment confirms a finding is gone, delete bot-only threads without
replies and resolve threads with human replies instead, preserving the
discussion. Skipped, disabled, cancelled, or incomplete checks never
prove a finding is gone.

Limits are one fixed, documented per-PR review-thread limit without a
consumer setting and with no fresh allowance per job/rerun. Failure
contributing findings win with deterministic ordering, not job completion
order. Full reports retain every finding; the summary distinguishes
findings omitted due to the limit from those without a valid diff
location. The numeric limit and thread-accounting mechanics are not yet
frozen.

Fork runs use the native all_external_contributors approval policy, not
first-time-only approval or a custom bot; outside authors cannot
self-approve. Approval permits execution but does not give fork code
secrets or write credentials. The fork-safe coverage comment carries the
dx-coverage-summary coverage marker with dedup, skips on Fork PR detected
so fork code never gets write credentials, and keeps privileged reporting
separate so it never executes fork-controlled code. Treat artifacts and
PR metadata as untrusted with a trusted reporting handoff.

Sensitive content stays least-privilege (contents read, checks write,
pull-requests write, nine persist-credentials false checkouts) and never
authorizes exposing credentials or secret values. Public CI reporting is
not confidential and is not a private vulnerability channel, without
claiming an unqualified generic redaction guarantee.

Retries use GitHub's native rerun controls, not bot comment commands,
without bot comment commands and without retrying analyzer failures until
green. Bounded transient reporting-transport retries may reuse the same
identified results; exhausted retries retain reporting failure.

Code Scanning publication is opt-in via code_scanning_opt_in, off by
default, with no upload-sarif wiring in the reusable workflow. Default
reporting works without Code Scanning permissions. Preserve the SARIF
completeness contract: complete scans stay eligible for authoritative
upload even when findings fail; incomplete scans never replace
authoritative scans. Disabled publication is not a reporting failure.

Sequential stays qualification-open: the template schedules parallel
only, platforms-gate fails closed on scheduling_mode sequential (and on
any other non-parallel value), and the mode input stays declared so
callers keep one stable interface when sequential qualifies.

Tag hygiene is as-built: version 0.0.0 with no v* tags, /dist/ plus
/release/ ignored, release_hygiene plus publish_trust harnesses wired,
with no publication pressure. Release inputs are reviewed pins only:
the caller pins reusable-consumer.yml at a full 40-hex SHA that must
match the consumer MODULE.bazel pin, with no silent upgrades. Tag
hygiene and release-input gaps stay recorded in the roadmap. Native-bot
follow-ups stay sole updater plus native-only with no third-party
updater retained (issue #461).

Build-only self-call forever stays rejected per #408; copy-pasted per
host jobs and waiting for all hosts stay rejected per #415; silent
upgrades, reviewdog, and bot commits stay rejected.

Seed only for platform plus consumer plus release evidence; no
Supported claim.
